# YGGDRASIL_GENOME_RELEASE_DESCRIPTION_VGP_STYLE v0.1
This genome was already submitted to GenomeArk or is intended for this.

Haplotype files:
	Haplotypes can be rep+alt, mat+pat or  hap1+hap2

	*rep.cur<date>.fasta.gz - representative (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid containg both sex chromosomes, as well as mtDNA
	*alt.cur<date>.fasta.gz - second (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid, but without any of sex chromosomes and mtDNA

	*mat.cur<date>.fasta.gz - maternal (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid (contains X for mammal or W for birds, for example), as well as mtDNA
 	*pat.cur<date>.fasta.gz - paternal (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid (contains Y for mammal or Z for birds, for example), no mtDNA

 	*hap1.cur<date>.fasta.gz - hap1 (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid (sex chromosomes are unknown or undescribed for species, or a ZZ/XX individual)
 	*hap2.cur<date>.fasta.gz - hap2 (pseudo)haplotype of a diploid (sex chromosomes are unknown or undescribed for species, or a ZZ/XX individual)

 	*hap0.cur<date>.fasta.gz - consensus pseudohaplotype of a diploid or a single haplotype of the haploid

Other files:
    *.len              - lengths of scaffolds
    *.reorderlist      - scaffold ids sorted in the same order as in the corresponding fasta file. Contains chromosomal scaffolds, attached to them unlocalized scaffolds and mtDNA
    *.chromosomes      - per-scaffold Sanger-style description of chromosomal and attached to them unlocalized scaffolds
    *.description      - per-scaffold NCBI style descriptions
    *.orderlist        - orderlist of scaffolds for visualization in MACE
    *.whitelist        - whitelist of scaffolds for visualizations in MACE. Usually contains only chromosomal scaffolds.
    *.evaluation       - assembly metrics. Contains values for all haplotypes

